e degree at the Auburn University College of Veterinary Medicine. He went on to earn a Master of Science degree from Texas A&M University and later completed a radiology residency at the Texas A&M University College of Veterinary Medicine.\nDr. King’s professional interests include the use of advanced, targeted radiation therapy to help pets with cancer maintain comfort and the best possible quality of life. He values the opportunity to walk alongside pets and their families during challenging moments, providing individualized care plans, compassionate guidance, and clear communication throughout their care journey.\nOutside of the hospital, Dr. Glen King enjoys playing golf and spending time outdoors.\nEducation & Training\nBachelor of Science:\nMississippi State University\nDoctor of Veterinary Medicine:\nAuburn University College of Veterinary Medicine\nMaster of Science:\nTexas A&M University\nResidency (Radiology):\nTexas A&M University College of Veterinary Medicine\nSpecializations\nBoard Certification:\nDiplomate, American College of Veterinary Radiology – Radiation Oncology\nAssociations\nAmerican College of Veterinary Radiology (ACVR)\nAmerican Veterinary Cancer Society (AVCS)\nAmerican Veterinary Medical Association (AVMA)\nTexas Veterinary Medical Association (TVMA)\nAwards & Recognition\nVice-Chairman, Texas Radiation Advisory Board\nMember, American College of Veterinary Radiology Exam Committee\nSpecialties\nRadiation Oncology\nServicing Locations\nMedVet Norwalk\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardi